    {
      "source_number": "186",
      "independent_solution": "Panel (a): the closed disk x^2+y^2<=4 intersected with the two exterior half-planes x<=-1 OR x>=1. Equivalently x^2+y^2<=4 AND x^2>=1; also a union of the two systems {x^2+y^2<=4,x<=-1} and {x^2+y^2<=4,x>=1}. The intersection x<=-1 AND x>=1 is empty and cannot replace the cap union; |x|<=1 selects the unhatched central strip. Solid arcs and chords are included. Panel (b): the upper bounding line is y=-x+1 and lower bounding line is y=x+1. The closed left wedge is the intersection y>=x+1 AND y<=-x+1. Conjunction entails x<=0, so the right branches do not create a second wedge. (-1,1) is inside, (1,1) outside, and (0,1) is the included apex. Half-unit grid spacing makes the circle radius 2 and wedge ordinate 1.",
